.TH PGXBACKUP 1 "April 2026" "pgxbackup 2.59.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pgxbackup \- reliable PostgreSQL backup and restore
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pgxbackup
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pgxbackup
is a backup and restore solution for PostgreSQL that scales to the largest
databases and workloads. It is a continuity fork of pgBackRest, on-disk
format compatible with upstream pgBackRest 2.58.
.PP
This is a stub manpage. Comprehensive command and option documentation is
served by the binary itself, via the
.B help
command.
.SH HELP
For general help and the list of commands:
.PP
.RS 4
.B pgxbackup help
.RE
.PP
For command-specific help:
.PP
.RS 4
.B pgxbackup help \fICOMMAND\fR
.RE
.PP
For option-specific help in the context of a command:
.PP
.RS 4
.B pgxbackup help \fICOMMAND\fR \fIOPTION\fR
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pgxbackup/pgxbackup.conf
Default configuration file location.
.TP
.I /etc/pgxbackup/conf.d/
Drop-in configuration directory; files matching
.B *.conf
are merged into the main configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/pgbackrest.conf
Legacy configuration file from upstream pgBackRest. Read for backward
compatibility if the per-distro default is absent.
.TP
.I /var/lib/pgxbackup/
Default repository path (overridable per stanza).
.TP
.I /var/log/pgxbackup/
Default log directory.
.TP
.I /var/spool/pgxbackup/
Default async-archive spool directory.
.SH AUTHORS
pgxbackup is maintained by pgExperts, Inc. as a continuity fork of
pgBackRest. The original pgBackRest was authored by David Steele and
contributors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pgbackrest (1)
if the upstream package is also installed; the two are on-disk format
compatible.
